Feature_01 volatility_20d_ann_pct is stddev_samp of simple returns over 20 rows (confirmed in the live refresh_feature_01_stock_daily definition), while I33 uses the population stdev of log returns. Against TS hist_vol on 20 tickers (28,319 bars):
- per-ticker medians run from 2.4% to 3.4% (overall 2.76%, roughly the sqrt(20/19) = 1.026 sample-to-population factor);
- p95 is 6.9%;
- the maximum is 23.2% (ACST).
The auditor's 'median 0.25-3%, max 14%' understates the gap.
